# {{WORKSPACE_NAME}}

{{One or two sentences: what this workspace is for and who shares it.}}

This is a shared agentic product workspace, stood up from Nava's Agentic Workspace Starter Kit. It gives the team and their agents shared context, boundaries, and reusable procedures.

## Getting started (new teammate)

1. Get the workspace onto your machine (git clone or Drive sync — see the team's chosen method below).
2. Install dependencies for the current phase (see the kit's `docs/local-setup.md`).
3. Point your agent tool at this folder (Claude Code reads `CLAUDE.md`; OpenCode/Codex/Cursor read `AGENTS.md`).
4. If `agentic-support/skills/` exists, run the skill sync script once.
5. Copy `bindings.env.template` to `bindings.env` and set your local paths.
6. Ask your agent to read the root `AGENTS.md` and the product area you're working in.

## Layout

- `canonical/` — reviewed, source-of-truth product work.
- `prototyping/` — spikes and experiments.
- `agentic-support/` — shared skills and Context Fabric (Walk phase and up).
- `docs/` — standard lanes: `ideation/`, `plans/`, `solutions/`.

Directory names follow lowercase kebab-case. See the kit's `docs/directory-and-naming-standard.md`.

